2026-09-23T21:05:48.609703Z [] {'source_reference_id': 'GO8455', 'source_id': 'grantconnect', 'title': 'Integrated Carer Support Service: Carer Gateway Service Providers (CGSPs)', 'source_url': None, 'issuing_agency': 'Department of Health, Disability and Ageing', 'category': 'Open Competitive', 'status': 'Open', 'publish_date': '2026-07-01', 'closing_date': '2026-09-24', 'value_amount': 951732965.0, 'value_currency': 'AUD', 'value_notes': 'GST exclusive', 'location': 'ACT, NSW, VIC, SA, WA, QLD, NT, TAS', 'description': 'This grant opportunity (GO8455) aims to select providers to deliver comprehensive support services for unpaid carers across 19 designated service areas in Australia. Services include carer support planning, in-person peer support, in-person counselling, in-person carer coaching, tailored supports (one-off practical support up to $1,500 or tailored packages up to $5,000 over 12 months), coordinated access to emergency respite care, and pre-employment training and support. Providers must deliver all listed service types, either directly or through subcontracting/brokerage, and are expected to establish and maintain at least one physical presence per service area.\n\nTotal funding available is $951,732,965.00 (GST exclusive) over five years, from 1 July 2027 to 30 June 2032. Funding is allocated per service area based on estimated carer populations, with weighting for remote areas and specific cohorts like First Nations and CALD carers. Establishment funding for new providers may commence as early as March 2027, with service delivery for all grantees starting 1 July 2027. Providers must operate Monday to Friday, 8am to 8pm.\n\nApplicants must use Attachment Pack Version 2 for their submissions. Multiple applications are permitted per service area (individual or as a lead consortium member), but only one will be selected. Eligibility requires compliance with specific legislation, including the National Redress Scheme, Workplace Gender Equality Act, and NDIS Act banning orders. Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) include call wait times for the national 1800 number (70% answered within 60 seconds, <5% abandonment rate, 24/7), time between intake and first planned service (7-28 days depending on urgency), and targets for carer satisfaction and improved wellbeing. No referee reports are required.', 'summary_headline': 'Department of Health, Disability and Ageing seeks Carer Gateway Service Providers for 19 service areas across Australia.', 'contact_name': None, 'contact_email': 'Grant.ATM@health.gov.au', 'contact_phone': '1300484145', 'lodgment_address': 'Online Application Form document located via the "Grant Opportunity Documents" button on the left-hand side.', 'documents': [{'file_name': 'Addendum 2 - Attachment Pack - GO8455 - Integrated Carer Support Service - Carer Gateway Service Providers.pdf.txt', 'extracted_text': " \n \nAmendment to the Integrated Carer Support Service: Carer \nGateway Service Providers (CGSPs) Grant Opportunity \nGO8455 - Addendum Number 2 \nDate Issued: 31 July 2026 \nThis addendum amends Grant Opportunity GO8455. The amendment is outlined below and applies \nfrom the date of publication. \nThe department apologises for any inconvenience caused by this administrative oversight and \nappreciates applicants' understanding and cooperation in responding to the updated requirements. \nUpdate to the Attachment Pack: \nAn updated Attachment Pack (Version 2) has been published and must be used for all applications. \nVersion 2 replaces the Attachment Pack that was published on GrantConnect on 1 July 2026. \nTo be considered for funding under GO8455, applicants must complete and submit their application \nusing Version 2 of the Attachment Pack, which is available in the Grant Opportunity documents on \nGrantConnect. \nThe updated Attachment Pack ensures that all applicants are assessed against the same \nrequirements and information, supporting a fair, transparent and equitable assessment process. \nApplications submitted using the previous version of the Attachment Pack will need to be withdrawn. \nImportant Information for Applicants: \nVersion 2 contains changes to the Attachment Pack published on 1 July 2026. Applicants should \ncarefully review the updated Attachment Pack and complete all required sections. \nApplicants are strongly encouraged not to copy and paste content directly from the previous version \ninto Version 2 without first reviewing the updated requirements. This will help ensure that all required \ninformation is provided and that the application can be properly assessed. \nApplicants Who Have Already Applied \nIf you applied using the Attachment Pack published on 1 July 2026, you must: \n1. Withdraw your submitted application; and \n2. Submit a new application using Version 2 of the Attachment Pack before the application \nclosing date. \nApplications submitted using the previous version of the Attachment Pack will not be considered for \nassessment unless they are withdrawn and resubmitted using Version 2. \n\nAddendum 2 ? GO8455 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n2 \n \nIn recognition that some applicants may be close to submitting their application when this Addendum \nis published, the department will monitor applications submitted between 31 July 2026 and 5pm AEST \nFriday 14 August 2026 for use of the previous version of the Attachment Pack. Applicants who submit \nup to 5pm AEST Friday 14 August 2026 using the previous version of the Attachment Pack will be \nnotified their applications will not be considered for assessment unless they are withdrawn and \nresubmitted using Version 2. After this date, it will be assumed that all applications submitted are \nusing Version 2 of the Attachment Pack. \nThe department apologises for the additional effort this may require and thanks applicants for their \nunderstanding and cooperation. \n\n"}, {'file_name': 'Addendum 2 - Attachment Pack - GO8455 - Integrated Carer Support Service - Carer Gateway Service Providers.txt', 'extracted_text': " \n \nAmendment to the Integrated Carer Support Service: Carer \nGateway Service Providers (CGSPs) Grant Opportunity \nGO8455 - Addendum Number 2 \nDate Issued: 31 July 2026 \nThis addendum amends Grant Opportunity GO8455. The amendment is outlined below and applies \nfrom the date of publication. \nThe department apologises for any inconvenience caused by this administrative oversight and \nappreciates applicants' understanding and cooperation in responding to the updated requirements. \nUpdate to the Attachment Pack: \nAn updated Attachment Pack (Version 2) has been published and must be used for all applications. \nVersion 2 replaces the Attachment Pack that was published on GrantConnect on 1 July 2026. \nTo be considered for funding under GO8455, applicants must complete and submit their application \nusing Version 2 of the Attachment Pack, which is available in the Grant Opportunity documents on \nGrantConnect. \nThe updated Attachment Pack ensures that all applicants are assessed against the same \nrequirements and information, supporting a fair, transparent and equitable assessment process. \nApplications submitted using the previous version of the Attachment Pack will need to be withdrawn. \nImportant Information for Applicants: \nVersion 2 contains changes to the Attachment Pack published on 1 July 2026. Applicants should \ncarefully review the updated Attachment Pack and complete all required sections. \nApplicants are strongly encouraged not to copy and paste content directly from the previous version \ninto Version 2 without first reviewing the updated requirements. This will help ensure that all required \ninformation is provided and that the application can be properly assessed. \nApplicants Who Have Already Applied \nIf you applied using the Attachment Pack published on 1 July 2026, you must: \n1. Withdraw your submitted application; and \n2. Submit a new application using Version 2 of the Attachment Pack before the application \nclosing date. \nApplications submitted using the previous version of the Attachment Pack will not be considered for \nassessment unless they are withdrawn and resubmitted using Version 2. \n\nAddendum 2 ? GO8455 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n2 \n \nIn recognition that some applicants may be close to submitting their application when this Addendum \nis published, the department will monitor applications submitted between 31 July 2026 and 5pm AEST \nFriday 14 August 2026 for use of the previous version of the Attachment Pack. Applicants who submit \nup to 5pm AEST Friday 14 August 2026 using the previous version of the Attachment Pack will be \nnotified their applications will not be considered for assessment unless they are withdrawn and \nresubmitted using Version 2. After this date, it will be assumed that all applications submitted are \nusing Version 2 of the Attachment Pack. \nThe department apologises for the additional effort this may require and thanks applicants for their \nunderstanding and cooperation. \n\n"}, {'file_name': 'Attachment Pack - GO8455 - Integrated Carer Support Service - Carer Gateway Service Providers - Version 2.xlsx.txt', 'extracted_text': '## Sheet: Business Model\n\tBusiness Model\t\t\t\t\n\tGrant Name - GO8455\t\t\t\t\n\tGuidance: Complete the name and ABN of your organisation along with the details of the service area you are applying for. All content must relate to the grant activity to be funded under this application process if successful. Please create a copy of this sheet named "Business Model - <service area>" for every service area applied for and identify where service delivery will benefit from economies of scale. Complete all fields in Purple in the table to describe your plan for establishing (where relevant) and maintaining your business model in each service area you are applying for, as it relates to Carer Gateway service delivery, governance, leadership and management, and working in partnership with the community. Each field has a character limit of 900 characters (approximately 150 words). Do not add more rows to the table. Refer to the grant opportunity guidelines and the Carer Gateway Service Provider Operating Manual for further guidance.\t\t\t\t\n\t<Insert Organisation name & ABN here>\t\t\t<Specify the service area this template relates to>\t\n\t\t\t\t<if applying for more than one service area, specify the other areas you are applying for>\t\n\tCARER GATEWAY SERVICE DELIVERY\t\t\t\t\n\tConsider here: How you will address identified priority carer needs in your region/communities including priority cohorts identified in the National Carer Strategy.\t\t\t\t\n\tObjective(s)\nWhat are you trying to achieve (outcome focused)? \tStrategy(ies)/Activity(ies)\nHow will you do this? \tPerformance Indicator(s)\nHow will you measure performance? \tTarget(s)\nWhat are your targets?\tTimeframe(s)\nWhen will this be delivered each year? \n\tCarer support planning\nAn intake and needs assessment process for the carer consistent with the Carer Support Framework in order to determine the services which best suit the needs of individual carers. \t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\n\tIn person peer support \nFree facilitated peer support forums and activities specifically designed to assist carers to improve their social connectedness, help them connect with people in similar circumstnaces in a safe environment and learn from peers to positively support carers\' emotional wellbeing. \t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\n\tIn-person counselling \nA free counselling service for carers who are experiencing difficulties with anxiety, stress, depression and low mood as a result of their caring role. The service will assist carers to manage their own health in order to remain effective in their caring role and avoid crisis events through in-person counselling sessions with a professional counsellor. \t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\n\tIn-person carer coaching\nA free psychoeducational service specifically desgined to assist carers to acquire the skills and resilience needed in their caring role. Service providers may deliver the \'in-person\' coaching face-to-face, via phone, or via digital channels such as video-calling. \t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\n\tTailored Supports \nDetermined by the agreed carer needs assessments to support carers in their caring role by providing a package of tailored supports and services that are inclusive, flexible, timely and based on the carer\'s level of need, where they live and that are culturally safe. The service is delivered in 2 formats - through the provision of (a) one-off practical supports or (b) a tailored support package. \t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\n\tCoordinated access to emergency respite care\nCoordinates access and referrals to emergency respite supports for carers who are experiencing an urgent, unplanned and imminent event that temporarily restricts their ability to continue caring when no other services are available. CGSPs will assist carers to access local supports and services and, if they see a need, they will work with local providers to undertake functions such as managing respite bookings.\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\n\tVocational Pathways\nProvision of vocational support includes in-house or brokered skills training (resume writing, interview skills, etc); and/or provides carers with access to Registered Training Organisations (RTO) accredited training (e.g. Cert II to IV) and/or provides carers with case management to support successful completion of training ? including goals, identified needs to support attendance at training, etc. \t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\n\tGOVERNANCE, LEADERSHIP AND MANAGEMENT\t\t\t\t\n\tConsider here: Senior Management and Board expertise; workforce development, strategic planning, accreditation (where relevant), quality assurance and governance; financial, IT, communication, reporting and client information systems; infrastructure; business risks and mitigation; carer needs and service planning. \t\t\t\t\n\tObjective(s)\nWhat are you trying to achieve (outcome focused)? \tStrategy(ies)/Activity(ies)\nHow will you do this? \tPerformance Indicator(s)\nHow will you measure performance? \tTarget(s)\nWhat are your targets?\tTimeframe(s)\nWhen will this be delivered? \n\tGovernance\nEnter details here regarding the governance arrangements which will be in place to monitor and maintain delivery of grant requirements.\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\n\tWorkforce Planning\nEnter details here regarding the workforce that will be  in place to deliver CGSP activities. This should include the planned approach to maintaining appropriate staffing and corporate knowledge.\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\n\tInfrastructure\nEnter details here regarding the infrastructure arrangements (both ICT and non-ICT related) which will be in place and how they will be maintained. \nRefer to section 6 of the CGSP Operating Manual for a list of the infrastructure requirements for CGSPs. \t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\n\tOperating guidelines and policies \nEnter details here regarding how the policies at section 4.5 of the Grant Opportunity Guidelines and section 7.2 of theCGSP Operating Manual will be maintained to support high quality service provision throughout the life of the grant agreement.\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\n\tContinuous Improvement\nEnter details here regarding how you will invest in innovation and continuous improvement activities to improve carer outcomes and contribute to the objectives of the National Carer Strategy 2024-2034 and associated Action Plan 2024-2027.\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\n\tWORKING IN PARTNERSHIP WITH THE COMMUNITY\t\t\t\t\n\tConsider here: Mechanisms to consult with community members on planning, design and implementation of services; community and client feedback and complaint processes; information dissemination to community around carer issues and service performance.\t\t\t\t\n\tObjective(s)\nWhat are you trying to achieve (outcome focused)? \tStrategy(ies)/Activity(ies)\nHow will you do this? \tPerformance Indicator(s)\nHow will you measure performance? \tTarget(s)\nWhat are your targets?\tTimeframe(s)\nWhen will this be delivered? \n\tService Area Planning and Outreach\nService providers must, on an annual basis, undertake a service area mapping exercise of their service area/s. The purpose of this mapping is to identify organisations delivering services which may be of benefit to carers, and to develop relationships with these organisations for the purpose of referring carers to these services. It is expected that service providers will need to utilise a wide range of existing services to meet the needs of carers.\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\n\tPromotion of Additional Carer Services\nService providers are responsible for undertaking promotional and profile-raising activities, including outreach activities to targeted groups such as young carers. This should include outreach activities within local communities and with local service providers. \nOutreach activities should also include promotion of online Carer Gateway services such as the\nself-guided carer coaching service, online carer skills courses and the online community forum.\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\n\tESTABLISHMENT (not required if your organisation currently receives grant funding to deliver Carer Gateway services in the service area you are applying for)\t\t\t\t\n\tConsider here: How you will ensure full operational readiness by 1 July 2027, assuming an approximately three-month establishment period.\t\t\t\t\n\tObjective(s)\nWhat are you trying to achieve (outcome focused)? \tStrategy(ies)/Activity(ies)\nHow will you do this? \tPerformance Indicator(s)\nHow will you measure performance? \tTarget(s)\nWhat are your targets?\tTimeframe(s)\nWhen will this be delivered? \n\tGovernance\nEnter details here regarding the governance arrangements which will be put in place to monitor progress toward delivery of the establishment plan.\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\n\tWorkforce Planning\nEnter details here regarding the workforce that will be put in place to deliver CGSP activities. This should include the planned approach to onboarding and training staff.\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\n\tInfrastructure\nEnter details here regarding the infrastructure arrangements (both ICT and non-ICT related) which will be put in place and how they will be established. \nRefer to section 6 of the CGSP Operating Manual for a list of the infrastructure requirements for CGSPs. \t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\n\tOperating guidelines and policies \nEnter details here regarding how the policies at section 4.5 of the grant opportunity guidlines and section 7.2 of the operating manual will be developed and implemented to support high quality service provision within the first 6 months of operating.\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\n\tTransition planning\nEnter details here regarding how you will work with the incumbent CGSP in the service area to transition carers information and service delivery whilst ensuring continuity of service.\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\n\n## Sheet: Budget\nIndicative Activity Budget\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\nGrant Name - GO8455\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n<Enter Organisation Name & ABN here>\t\t<Enter the name of the proposed service area here>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\nGuidance: Include a detailed budget per region by providing clear costings (include the source/basis of the estimates) for essential budget items outlined below. Please create a copy of this sheet named "Budget - <service area>" for every service area applied for and clearly indicate where benefits will result from economies of scale. Each field has a character limit of 900 characters (approximately 150 words). Do not add more rows to the table. Please ensure all figures are GST Exclusive. \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\nOperational Expenses\t\tNotes/basis of estimate/breakdown of items \n(e.g. 2 full time staff members, Software updates for system, etc.)\tEstablishment \n$ GST Excl.\n(only complete where  estabishment funds are required separate to 2027/28 funding)\t2027/28\n$ GST Excl.\t2028/29\n$ GST Excl.\t2029/30\n$ GST Excl.\t2030/31\n$ GST Excl.\t2031/32\n$ GST Excl.\tTOTAL\n$ GST Excl.\t\t\t\t\t\nDirect FTE\tSalaries / Wages\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\n\tOn-Costs\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\n\tRegional and remote costs\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\n\tOther\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\nIndirect FTE\tSalaries / Wages\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\n\tOn-Costs\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\n\tRegional and remote costs\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\n\tOther\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\nService Delivery\tClient Support Services \t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\n\tClient Support consumables\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\n\tTraining & Development (excl Board / Governance)\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\n\tConsultants/Sub-Contractors\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t\t\t\t\t\t\nInfrastructure\tRent\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\n\tUtilities\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\n\tCommunications & IT including software and hardware\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\n\tInsurance (excl Motor Vehicle)\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\n\tMotor Vehicle Expenses (incl Insurance and Repairs & Maintenance)\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\nAdministrative\tHR / Corporate Services\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\tAccounting / Audit fees\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\n\tAdvertising & Promotion\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\n\tBoard / Governance (Travel, Accommodation & Training) \t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\n\tDepreciation\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\n\tRepairs & Maintenance (excl Motor Vehicles)\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\n\tTravel & Accommodation (excl Board / Governance)\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\nOther Expenses (please include source, and list each separately - add rows)\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t0\t\t\t\t\t\nTotal Operational Expenses\t\t\t\t0\t0\t0\t0\t0\t0\t\t\t\t\t\n\n## Sheet: Risk Management Plan\nRisk Management Plan\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\nGrant Name - GO8455\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n<Insert Organisation name & ABN here>\t\t\t\t\t<Enter the name of your grant activity here>\t\t\t\t\nGuidance: Complete all fields in Green in the table for risk associated with all regions you are applying for under this grant opportunity on a single page. Do not create a copy of this sheet for each service area applied for. Each field has a character limit of 900 characters (approximately 150 words). You must complete a minimum of three and no more than 5 risks. An example risk has been filled out in the first row. Please use the "Risk Information & Help" tab (next tab) for further guidance and examples.\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\nRisk Reference\tRisk\tRisk Identification (Source)\nWhat event(s) can happen and how it can happen?\tRisk Impact\nWhat are the effects if it does happen?\tRisk Controls\nWhat is currently in place to manage the risk?\tLikelihood\tConsequence\tCurrent risk rating\tAcceptable/ unacceptable?  \tRisk Treatments\nWhat (if any) additional work is planned or underway to manage the risk?\nExample\tPeople Management\t?\tInadequate mechanisms for staff accountability and performance management.\n?\tInadequate support for mental health issues resulting in increased stress levels and burnout among \nemployees. \n?\tInability to hire and maintain staff with the right skills. \t?\tHigher absenteeism\n?\tDecreased productivity\n?\tDiminished morale\n?\tDelays or inability to deliver Carer Gateway supports and services.\t?\tRegular team and 1:1 staff meetings to discuss performance and raise potential issues early.\n?\tEAP available to all staff.\n?\tLimits placed on staff working hours to prevent burnout. \n?\tPermanent staff have appropriate annual and personal leave entitlements.\n?\tCompetitive salaries and benefits packages attract and retain skilled staff.\tUnlikely\tMinor\tLow\tAcceptable \t?\tRisk has been rated acceptable, no further treatments required or planned.\n1\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\tChoose an item.\tChoose an item.\tChoose an item.\tChoose an item.\t<insert>\n2\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\tChoose an item.\tChoose an item.\tChoose an item.\tChoose an item.\t<insert>\n3\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\tChoose an item.\tChoose an item.\tChoose an item.\tChoose an item.\t<insert>\n4\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\tChoose an item.\tChoose an item.\tChoose an item.\tChoose an item.\t<insert>\n5\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\t<insert>\tChoose an item.\tChoose an item.\tChoose an item.\tChoose an item.\t<insert>\n\n## Sheet: Risk Information & Help\n\tRisk Information & Help\t\t\t\t\t\n\tRISKS\nA risk is defined as the effect of uncertainty on objectives1.  A risk is often expressed in terms of a combination of the consequences of an event (including changes in circumstances or knowledge) and the associated likelihood of occurrence.  \nWhere possible, try to combine similar risks to consolidate the number of potential risks.\t\t\t\t\t\n\tRISK IDENTIFICATION (SOURCE)\nThe purpose of risk identification is to find, recognise and describe risks that might prevent an organisation achieving its objectives. When identifying risks the following questions should be considered;\n? What event(s) can happen that will have an adverse effect on the activity?\n? How can it happen?\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\tRISK IMPACT\nThe impact identifies the consequence of each risk (i.e. what are the effects to your organisation if it risk does happen?).\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\tRISK CONTROL\nA control is a current process, policy, device, practice or any other action designed to modify risk. Examples of controls include, checklists, meetings, procedures manual, contingency plans, audits and agreements in place.\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\tRISK TREATMENT\nA risk treatment is an additional activity being developed to manage and/or reduce the risk.  Examples of risk treatments include the creation of new guidelines, the introduction of a review process etc. Once the proposed treatment has been implemented it becomes a control.\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\tEFFECTIVENESS OF RISK IDENTIFICATION\nAn adequate control implies that the risk is well managed and no further treatments are required.\nA marginally effective control implies that a treatment is not necessary however this may depend on the level of risk.\nAn inadequate control implies that treatments are necessary.\t\t\t\t\t\n\tLIKELIHOOD\nLikelihood is the chance that something might happen. Likelihood can be defined, determined, or measured objectively or subjectively and can be expressed either qualitatively or quantitatively (using mathematics).\nRate the likelihood of the identified risk occurring with the controls in place.\nRatings are: Almost certain, Likely, Possible, Unlikely or Rare.\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\tCONSEQUENCE\nA consequence is the outcome of an event and has an effect on objectives. \nRate the consequence to the Project outcomes of the identified risk occurring with the controls in place.\nRatings are: Insignificant, Minor, Moderate, Major or Catastrophic.\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t1Further information at: \tRisk Management - Principles and Guidelines 2018\t\t\t\t\n\tCURRENT RISK RATINGS\t\t\t\t\t\n\tLikelihood\tInsignificant Consequences\tMinor Consequences\tModerate Consequences\tMajor Consequences\tCatastrophic Consequences\n\tAlmost Certain\tLow\tMedium\tHigh\tExtreme\tExtreme\n\tLikely\tLow\tMedium\tHigh\tHigh\tExtreme\n\tPossible\tLow\tMedium\tMedium\tHigh\tExtreme\n\tUnlikely\tLow\tLow\tMedium\tMedium\tHigh\n\tRare\tLow\tLow\tMedium\tMedium\tMedium\n\tEXAMPLES OF RISK\t\t\t\t\t\n\tRisk\tLikelihood\nLow/Medium/High\n(comments)\tImpact\nLow/Medium/High\tMitigation Strategies\t\t\n\tDelays in receiving funding\te.g. Low\tHigh/Med/Low\tEnsure project deliverables are achieved in line with project plan and reported to the department in a timely fashion.\t\t\n\tDelays in recruitment of staff\tMay depend on nature, complexity and size of project.\tHigh/Med/Low\tRealistic understanding of what can be achieved within a limited timeframe and budget and awareness of what staff are likely to be available. \t\t\n\tBudget shortfalls\tProject has been appropriately scoped to cover all known contingencies. Project will be fully funded by Grant.\tHigh/Med/Low\tDevelop budgets to fully plan for known likelihoods and factor in relevant contingencies. Take a competitive approach to the market.\t\t\n\tBudget underspends \tWhere project is not rolled out in a timely fashion or has been inappropriately scoped in relation to expenditure. \tHigh/Med/Low\tEnsure a realistic project plan, timeline and budget are in place.\t\t\n\tOperational demands lead to delays to the timely delivery of project\tMay depend on scope of project; availability of appropriate staff; unforeseen circumstances; inadequate planning; unrealistic goals.\tHigh/Med/Low\tEnsure project manager/coordinator is fully capable and is working to a realistic project plan, timeline and budget can be enshrined in the Funding Agreement.\t\t\n\tCommunication with staff and/or target population\tInadequate or inappropriate methods of communication leads to breakdown in roll out of project.\tHigh/Med/Low\tCommunication with staff is incorporated into management plan along with a stakeholder engagement plan.\t\t\n\tTarget populations do not response to project\tLow uptake of project by target population.\tHigh/Med/Low\tThorough needs assessment and response is part of the project proposal and evidence of both need and adequacy of response is identified in project plan. Ongoing marketing and flexible project delivery.\t\t\n\n## Sheet: Data\n\tLikelihood\t\t\t\n\tChoose an item\tConsequence\tCurrent Risk Rating\tAcceptable/Unacceptable?\n\tRare\tInsignificant\tLow\tAcceptable \n\tUnlikely\tMinor\tMedium\tUnacceptable\n\tPossible\tModerate\tHigh\t\n\tLikely\tMajor\tExtreme\t\n\tAlmost Certain\tCatastrophic\t\t'}, {'file_name': 'GO8455 - Integrated Carer Support Service - Carer Gateway Service Providers - CGSPs - Addendum 1.PDF.txt', 'extracted_text': ' \n \n \n \nAmendment to the Integrated Carer Support Service: Carer Gateway Service Providers \n(CGSPs) Opportunity \nGO8455 - Addendum Number 1 \n \nDate Issued: 15 July 2026  \nThis addendum is issued as an amendment to grant opportunity GO8455. The amendment is as specified hereunder. \nChanges to the Carer Gateway Service Framework \nDelete \nInsert \nNA \nInsert ?(see figure 1)? on page 3 of th